<div class=3D"resource-viewer-header"><div class=3D"resource-viewer-title-r=
ow"><h1 class=3D"resource-viewer-title"><span>Install the plugin</span></h1=
><div class=3D"resource-viewer-header-aside"></div></div></div><div class=
=3D"resource-viewer-body"><div class=3D"resource-viewer-column"><div class=
=3D"resource-viewer-prose"><p class=3D"md-paragraph"><em>In Cowork only.</e=
m></p>
<p class=3D"md-paragraph">Do this now <strong>Install the AI Employee Build=
er plugin in Claude.</strong></p>
<p class=3D"md-paragraph">Open <strong>Customize =E2=86=92 Personal plugins=
 =E2=86=92 + =E2=86=92 Add marketplace</strong>, then paste this marketplac=
e name:</p>
<p class=3D"md-paragraph"><code class=3D"md-inline-code">the2hourclo/aieb-t=
hin-plugin</code></p>
<h4 class=3D"md-header">Prefer to watch first? Open the 1-minute walkthroug=
h</h4>
<p class=3D"md-paragraph">Everything happens in the Claude <strong>desktop =
app</strong> (Pro, Max, or Team) =E2=80=94 no terminal, nothing to download=
.</p>
<p class=3D"md-paragraph"><strong>1.</strong> After you paste the marketpla=
ce name, click <strong>Sync</strong>.</p>
<p class=3D"md-paragraph"><strong>2.</strong> Install <strong>AI Employee B=
uilder</strong>. When it appears in your plugins, this step is complete.</p=
>
<p class=3D"md-paragraph"><strong>Already installed AIEB?</strong> Open <st=
rong>Browse plugins =E2=86=92 Personal =E2=86=92 aieb-thin-plugin</strong>,=
 click the <strong>three dots (=E2=80=A6)</strong>, then choose <strong>Che=
ck for updates</strong>. Return to <strong>Customize =E2=86=92 Plugins =E2=
=86=92 AI Employee Builder</strong> and click <strong>Update</strong> if th=
at button appears. After the update, continue below inside the Cowork Proje=
ct and folder where you want your workspace saved.</p>
<p class=3D"md-paragraph"><img src=3D"http://127.0.0.1:8797/sites/ai-employ=
ee-builders/media/assets/get-access/cowork-aieb-check-for-updates.png" alt=
=3D"The aieb-thin-plugin marketplace menu in Cowork with Check for updates =
selected"></p>
<p class=3D"md-paragraph"><strong>1. Refresh the marketplace:</strong> open=
 <strong>Browse plugins =E2=86=92 Personal =E2=86=92 aieb-thin-plugin</stro=
ng>, click the <strong>three dots (=E2=80=A6)</strong>, and choose <strong>=
Check for updates</strong>.</p>
<p class=3D"md-paragraph"><img src=3D"http://127.0.0.1:8797/sites/ai-employ=
ee-builders/media/assets/get-access/cowork-aieb-install-update.png" alt=3D"=
The installed AI Employee Builder plugin in Cowork showing the Update butto=
n"></p>
<p class=3D"md-paragraph"><strong>2. Install the update:</strong> return to=
 <strong>Customize =E2=86=92 Plugins =E2=86=92 AI Employee Builder</strong>=
 and click <strong>Update</strong> if the button appears.</p>
<p class=3D"md-paragraph"><strong>You'll see a red =E2=80=9Cmake sure you t=
rust this plugin=E2=80=9D notice.</strong> That's Claude's standard warning=
 for every non-Anthropic plugin =E2=80=94 this one is ours.</p>
<p class=3D"md-paragraph"><strong>Don't see =E2=80=9CPersonal plugins=E2=80=
=9D in Customize?</strong> Update the Claude desktop app first (quit and re=
open usually does it), then look again. On a managed Team/Enterprise accoun=
t, an admin may have to allow personal plugins first.</p></div></div></div>=
